\f0\fs24\b Let's Peppol eID Bridge\b0\fs22\par
\par
Connect your Belgian eID to Let's Peppol to approve signing requests. This installer includes the desktop application, runtime libraries and a private Belgian eID module.\par
\par
\b Browser setup\b0\par
The installer requests the official Web eID extension for Edge and Chrome. Save your work and restart your browser after installation, then enable Web eID when prompted. Firefox users install the extension from its official store. Onboarding provides the appropriate store link if needed.\par
\par
\b Support and logs\b0\par
Help: https://be.letspeppol.org/onboarding\par
Logging is enabled in Documents\'5cLetsPeppol eID Bridge\'5cLogs. Review logs before sharing them with support. Keep your PIN private.\par
\par
\b Open-source licences\b0\par
This application is based on Web eID and libelectronic-id (MIT). Belgian eID middleware and Qt are separate dynamically loaded libraries covered by their respective LGPL licences. Copyright notices, licence texts and source information are included in the licenses folder. Those licences govern the respective components; installation does not restrict the rights they grant.\par
\par
The original Web eID and Belgian government projects do not endorse this fork.\par
